using Kotlin data classes, the&nbsp;<code class=3D"mv6bHd">no-arg</code>&nb=
sp;compiler plugin can automatically generate a no-argument constructor for=
 your entities, satisfying the JPA requirement without manual declaration.<=
/span></p></li>
<li><p><span>Avoid using&nbsp;<code class=3D"mv6bHd">data class</code>&nbsp=
;for entities if it complicates no-arg constructor generation:&nbsp;</span>=
<br><span>While&nbsp;<code class=3D"mv6bHd">data class</code>&nbsp;is conve=
nient, if it makes it difficult to ensure a no-arg constructor for your ent=
ities, consider a regular class.</span></p></li>
<li><p><span><strong>Separate DTOs from Entities:</strong>&nbsp;</span><br>=
<span>DTOs should be distinct from your JPA entities to avoid confusion and=
